  '{0,2}',
  'Option A (correct) is Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, which can capture and store high-volume log data in real-time, allowing for subsequent processing and delivery to S3. Option C (correct) is Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, a fully managed service that can directly deliver streaming data, including logs, to Amazon S3 with optional transformations. Option B (incorrect) is for large-scale online data transfer between on-premises storage and AWS storage services, not for real-time log ingestion. Option D (incorrect) is a message queuing service, not optimized for direct high-volume log ingestion to S3. Option E (incorrect) is a physical device for offline data transfer.',
