VALUES (
  'q_46_m_46_2_81',
  'Which Amazon SageMaker feature allows for comparing different versions of a deployed model or different models to determine which performs better in a production environment, often used for gradual rollouts or testing new features?',
  'mcq',
  '["A/B testing with SageMaker endpoint production variants","Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor","Amazon SageMaker Pipelines","Amazon SageMaker Model Registry"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) is A/B testing with SageMaker endpoint production variants. This feature allows you to deploy multiple model versions or different models to a single endpoint, route a percentage of inference traffic to each, and compare their performance metrics to determine the best variant. Option B (incorrect) is Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor, which is for detecting data and model quality drift. Option C (incorrect) is Amazon SageMaker Pipelines, which automates ML workflows. Option D (incorrect) is Amazon SageMaker Model Registry, which is for versioning and managing models.',
