INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_46_m_46_1_97',
  'A data science team is preparing to store large datasets for machine learning model training in Amazon S3. They need to ensure data durability and cost-effectiveness for varying access patterns. Order the steps to configure an S3 bucket for optimal data lifecycle management.',
  'ordering',
  '["Define an S3 Lifecycle policy to transition objects to lower-cost storage classes.","Enable S3 Versioning on the bucket to protect against accidental deletions or overwrites.","Create an Amazon S3 bucket in the desired AWS Region.","Configure S3 bucket policies and IAM roles for secure access."]'::json,
  '{2,1,3,0}',
  'To properly set up an Amazon S3 bucket for ML data, Option C (Create an Amazon S3 bucket) is the foundational first step. Following this, Option B (Enable S3 Versioning) is crucial for data durability and recovery, protecting against unintended changes. Next, Option D (Configure S3 bucket policies and IAM roles) is essential for securing access to the data, ensuring only authorized users or services can interact with it. Finally, Option A (Define an S3 Lifecycle policy) should be applied to manage data cost-effectively by transitioning objects to appropriate storage classes based on access patterns, which relies on the bucket and its security being already in place.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain46_10',
  NOW(),
  7,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_46_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_46_m_46_1_98',
  'A machine learning project requires a shared file system for multiple Amazon EC2 instances used for data preprocessing. The file system needs to be highly available and scalable. Order the steps to set up an Amazon EFS file system for this purpose.',
  'ordering',
  '["Mount the Amazon EFS file system on the EC2 instances.","Create an Amazon EFS file system.","Configure security groups to allow inbound NFS traffic to the EFS mount targets.","Create mount targets for the EFS file system in the relevant VPC subnets."]'::json,
  '{1,3,2,0}',
  'The first step is Option B (Create an Amazon EFS file system), which initializes the shared storage. Next, Option D (Create mount targets) is necessary to provide network endpoints for EC2 instances to connect to EFS within specific subnets. Following this, Option C (Configure security groups) is critical to ensure that the EC2 instances can communicate with the EFS mount targets over NFS. Finally, Option A (Mount the Amazon EFS file system) is the last step, allowing the EC2 instances to access the shared storage.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain46_10',
  NOW(),
  8,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_46_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_46_m_46_1_99',
  'A data scientist needs to prepare a large dataset stored in Amazon S3 for training a SageMaker model. The data needs to be preprocessed and stored in a format optimized for training. Order the general steps for preparing this data.',
  'ordering',
  '["Store the processed data in an S3 bucket, optimized for SageMaker training.","Load the raw data from the source S3 bucket into a processing environment.","Perform data cleaning, transformation, and feature engineering.","Define the data schema and preprocessing requirements."]'::json,
  '{3,1,2,0}',
  'Option D (Define the data schema and preprocessing requirements) is the initial planning phase, crucial before any data manipulation. Next, Option B (Load the raw data) brings the data into an environment where it can be worked on. Following this, Option C (Perform data cleaning, transformation, and feature engineering) is the core preprocessing step. Finally, Option A (Store the processed data) is the last step, making the data available for model training.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain46_10',
  NOW(),
  9,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_46_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_46_m_46_1_100',
  'An organization needs to ensure that all sensitive machine learning training data stored in Amazon S3 is encrypted at rest using customer-managed keys. Order the steps to implement this security measure.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure the S3 bucket''s default encryption to use the created KMS key.","Upload training data to the S3 bucket.","Create an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) customer managed key (CMK).","Grant the SageMaker execution role permissions to use the KMS key."]'::json,
  '{2,0,3,1}',
  'Option C (Create an AWS KMS customer managed key) is the prerequisite for using customer-managed encryption. Once the key is available, Option A (Configure the S3 bucket''s default encryption) links the bucket to use this specific KMS key for all new objects. Next, Option D (Grant the SageMaker execution role permissions) ensures that the service or user interacting with the data has the necessary authorization to use the KMS key for encryption/decryption. Finally, Option B (Upload training data to the S3 bucket) can occur, and the data will be automatically encrypted using the configured KMS key.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain46_10',
  NOW(),
  10,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_46_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_46_m_46_1_101',
  'A data engineering team needs to set up a scalable and durable repository for model artifacts and processed features, which will be accessed by SageMaker training jobs. Order the steps to establish this data repository.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure S3 bucket policies to restrict access to authorized IAM roles.","Create a new Amazon S3 bucket dedicated to model artifacts and processed features.","Enable S3 Object Lock for compliance if immutability is required.","Upload model artifacts and processed features to the S3 bucket."]'::json,
  '{1,0,2,3}',
  'Option B (Create a new Amazon S3 bucket) is the initial step to provision the storage. Following this, Option A (Configure S3 bucket policies) is crucial for securing the bucket and ensuring only authorized entities can access the data. Option C (Enable S3 Object Lock) is an optional but important step for compliance or immutability requirements, which should be done before data is uploaded if it needs to be protected from modification or deletion. Finally, Option D (Upload model artifacts and processed features) is the action of populating the configured and secured bucket with the actual data.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain46_10',
  NOW(),
  11,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_46_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_46_m_46_1_102',
  'A company needs to store large volumes of historical data for machine learning analysis, with varying access patterns from frequent to archival. Order the steps to implement a cost-effective Amazon S3 storage solution.',
  'ordering',
  '["Upload historical data to the S3 bucket.","Create an S3 bucket in the appropriate AWS Region.","Implement S3 Intelligent-Tiering to automatically optimize storage costs.","Define IAM policies to control access to the S3 bucket."]'::json,
  '{1,3,2,0}',
  'Option B (Create an S3 bucket) is the fundamental first step. After the bucket is created, Option D (Define IAM policies) is essential for securing the data by controlling who can access it. To achieve cost-effectiveness for varying access patterns, Option C (Implement S3 Intelligent-Tiering) should be configured on the bucket. Finally, Option A (Upload historical data) is the last step, as the data will then benefit from the intelligent tiering and security configurations.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain46_10',
  NOW(),
  12,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_46_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_46_m_46_1_103',
  'A machine learning team is setting up a database to store metadata about their training jobs and models. They need a managed, scalable, and highly available relational database. Order the steps to provision an Amazon RDS instance for this purpose.',
  'ordering',
  '["Connect the SageMaker environment to the RDS instance.","Configure security groups to allow inbound traffic from the SageMaker VPC.","Launch an Amazon RDS database instance.","Create a database within the RDS instance for metadata storage."]'::json,
  '{2,1,3,0}',
  'Option C (Launch an Amazon RDS database instance) is the initial provisioning step for the database. Following this, Option B (Configure security groups) is crucial to establish network connectivity and allow authorized services like SageMaker to reach the database. Next, Option D (Create a database within the RDS instance) sets up the logical container for the metadata. Finally, Option A (Connect the SageMaker environment to the RDS instance) establishes the application-level connection.',
