  'quiz_domain46_10',
  NOW(),
  13,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_46_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_46_m_46_1_104',
  'A data lake for machine learning is being built using Amazon S3. To ensure data integrity and track changes, data versioning is a key requirement. Order the steps to enable and manage versioning for an S3 bucket.',
  'ordering',
  '["Retrieve previous versions of objects if needed.","Enable S3 Versioning on the target S3 bucket.","Upload objects to the version-enabled S3 bucket.","Configure S3 Lifecycle policies to manage old versions."]'::json,
  '{1,2,3,0}',
  'Option B (Enable S3 Versioning) is the foundational step to activate the feature on the bucket. Once versioning is enabled, Option C (Upload objects to the version-enabled S3 bucket) will automatically create new versions for each change. Following this, Option D (Configure S3 Lifecycle policies) helps manage the cost and retention of old versions. Finally, Option A (Retrieve previous versions) is the operational step taken when a specific older version of an object is required.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain46_10',
  NOW(),
  14,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_46_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_46_m_46_1_105',
  'A machine learning team needs to store large model artifacts that will be frequently accessed by SageMaker inference endpoints. They require low-latency access and high throughput. Order the steps to set up an Amazon S3 bucket optimized for this use case.',
  'ordering',
  '["Upload model artifacts to the S3 bucket.","Create an Amazon S3 bucket.","Configure S3 bucket policies to allow SageMaker inference endpoints access.","Ensure the S3 bucket is in the same AWS Region as the SageMaker endpoints."]'::json,
  '{1,3,2,0}',
  'Option B (Create an Amazon S3 bucket) is the initial step to provision the storage. Next, Option D (Ensure the S3 bucket is in the same AWS Region) is crucial for minimizing latency and optimizing data transfer costs for SageMaker inference. Following this, Option C (Configure S3 bucket policies) is necessary to grant the inference endpoints the required permissions to access the model artifacts. Finally, Option A (Upload model artifacts) is the last step, populating the bucket with the models.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain46_10',
  NOW(),
  15,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_46_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_46_m_46_1_106',
  'A financial institution is deploying a highly sensitive fraud detection model using Amazon SageMaker. The model training data and artifacts are stored in Amazon S3, and inference results are also written back to S3. The security team mandates that all data at rest must be encrypted with customer-managed keys (CMKs) and that SageMaker''s access to S3 must adhere strictly to the principle of least privilege, with auditability for all data operations.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure SageMaker training and inference jobs to use an IAM execution role with `s3:GetObject` and `s3:PutObject` permissions only on the specific S3 bucket prefixes for data and artifacts.","Create an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) Customer Managed Key (CMK) and configure the S3 buckets to use server-side encryption with KMS (SSE-KMS) for all objects.","Attach an IAM policy to the SageMaker execution role that allows `kms:Decrypt` and `kms:GenerateDataKey` on the specific KMS CMK.","Enable Amazon CloudTrail logging for S3 data events and KMS API calls to monitor access and encryption usage."]'::json,
  '{1,0,2,3}',
  'To meet the security requirements, the correct sequence of steps is to first establish the encryption mechanism, then configure SageMaker''s access to the data, then grant SageMaker the necessary KMS permissions, and finally enable monitoring. Option B (correct) is the foundational step of creating the KMS CMK and configuring S3 buckets for SSE-KMS, ensuring data at rest is encrypted with customer-managed keys. Option A (correct) then focuses on granting SageMaker least privilege access to the S3 data, which is dependent on the S3 buckets being ready. Option C (correct) provides the SageMaker execution role with the necessary permissions to use the KMS CMK for encryption and decryption, which is required for SageMaker to interact with the SSE-KMS encrypted data. Option D (correct) is the final step for auditability, enabling CloudTrail logging to monitor access and encryption usage.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain46_10',
  NOW(),
  16,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_46_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_46_m_46_1_107',
  'A data science team needs to securely store their machine learning training datasets in Amazon S3 and ensure that Amazon SageMaker training jobs can access them with the principle of least privilege. Arrange the following steps in the correct order to achieve this.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an IAM policy that grants read-only access to the specific S3 bucket and prefix.","Create an S3 bucket with server-side encryption enabled, using an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) key.","Attach the IAM policy to the SageMaker execution role.","Upload the training data to the designated S3 bucket prefix."]'::json,
  '{1,3,0,2}',
  'The correct sequence begins with establishing the secure storage. Option B (Create an S3 bucket with server-side encryption enabled, using an AWS KMS key) is the foundational step for secure data storage. Option D (Upload the training data to the designated S3 bucket prefix) follows, placing the data into the secured bucket. Option A (Create an IAM policy that grants read-only access to the specific S3 bucket and prefix) defines the necessary permissions, adhering to least privilege. Finally, Option C (Attach the IAM policy to the SageMaker execution role) applies these permissions to the entity that needs to access the data, making it available for SageMaker training jobs. Incorrect orders would either attempt to upload data before the bucket is ready, define permissions before the resource exists, or attach policies before they are defined.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain46_10',
  NOW(),
  17,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_46_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_46_m_46_1_108',
  'A machine learning engineer needs to ensure that all model artifacts generated by Amazon SageMaker training jobs are encrypted at rest using a customer-managed key. Arrange the following steps to configure this encryption.',
  'ordering',
  '["Specify the KMS key ARN in the ''OutputDataConfig'' when creating the SageMaker training job.","Create a customer-managed AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) key.","Grant the SageMaker execution role permissions to use the KMS key.","Configure the S3 bucket, where model artifacts will be stored, to use the KMS key for default encryption."]'::json,
  '{1,2,3,0}',
  'The process starts with creating the encryption key. Option B (Create a customer-managed AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) key) is the first logical step. Next, the SageMaker service needs permission to use this key, so Option C (Grant the SageMaker execution role permissions to use the KMS key) follows. Option D (Configure the S3 bucket, where model artifacts will be stored, to use the KMS key for default encryption) ensures that any objects written to the S3 bucket are encrypted by default with the specified key. Finally, Option A (Specify the KMS key ARN in the ''OutputDataConfig'' when creating the SageMaker training job) explicitly tells SageMaker to use this key for its output artifacts, overriding or reinforcing the bucket''s default encryption.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain46_10',
  NOW(),
  18,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_46_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_46_m_46_1_109',
  'To enhance security, a company mandates that all Amazon SageMaker training jobs run within a Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) without direct internet access. Arrange the following steps to configure VPC isolation for a SageMaker training job.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure security groups to allow necessary inbound and outbound traffic for the training job.","Create a VPC with private subnets and VPC endpoints for required AWS services (e.g., S3, ECR).","Specify the VPC ID and subnet IDs when launching the SageMaker training job.","Configure route tables for the private subnets to route traffic through the VPC endpoints and prevent internet access."]'::json,
  '{1,3,0,2}',
  'The initial step for VPC isolation is to set up the network environment. Option B (Create a VPC with private subnets and VPC endpoints for required AWS services) establishes the isolated network. Following this, Option D (Configure route tables for the private subnets to route traffic through the VPC endpoints and prevent internet access) defines how traffic flows within this isolated network. Option A (Configure security groups to allow necessary inbound and outbound traffic for the training job) then specifies the firewall rules for the compute instances within the subnets. Finally, Option C (Specify the VPC ID and subnet IDs when launching the SageMaker training job) instructs SageMaker to use this configured isolated environment for the training job.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain46_10',
  NOW(),
  19,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_46_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_46_m_46_1_110',
  'An MLOps team needs to establish a new IAM execution role for Amazon SageMaker that adheres to the principle of least privilege for accessing S3 data. Arrange the following steps to properly configure this role.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an IAM role with ''Amazon SageMaker'' as the trusted entity.","Attach a custom IAM policy to the role, granting specific S3 bucket and prefix permissions.","Define the specific S3 bucket and prefix where training data and model artifacts will be stored.","Review and verify the effective permissions of the IAM role."]'::json,
  '{0,2,1,3}',
  'The first step is to create the foundational IAM role. Option A (Create an IAM role with ''Amazon SageMaker'' as the trusted entity) sets up the role that SageMaker can assume. Before defining permissions, it''s crucial to know what resources need access, so Option C (Define the specific S3 bucket and prefix where training data and model artifacts will be stored) specifies the target resources. Then, Option B (Attach a custom IAM policy to the role, granting specific S3 bucket and prefix permissions) applies the fine-grained permissions. Lastly, Option D (Review and verify the effective permissions of the IAM role) is a critical security best practice to ensure the least privilege principle is correctly applied and no unintended access is granted.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain46_10',
  NOW(),
  20,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_46_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_46_m_46_1_111',
  'A machine learning project requires robust versioning for its model artifacts stored in Amazon S3, ensuring traceability and rollback capabilities. Arrange the following steps to enable and manage object versioning for SageMaker model artifacts.',
  'ordering',
  '["Enable versioning on the target Amazon S3 bucket where SageMaker stores model artifacts.","Upload new versions of model artifacts to the S3 bucket.","Retrieve a specific version of a model artifact using its version ID.","Configure SageMaker training jobs to output model artifacts to the versioned S3 bucket."]'::json,
  '{0,3,1,2}',
  'The process of managing versions starts with enabling the feature on the storage. Option A (Enable versioning on the target Amazon S3 bucket where SageMaker stores model artifacts) is the prerequisite. Once versioning is active, Option D (Configure SageMaker training jobs to output model artifacts to the versioned S3 bucket) ensures that SageMaker utilizes this feature. Option B (Upload new versions of model artifacts to the S3 bucket) represents the ongoing process of generating and storing new model iterations. Finally, Option C (Retrieve a specific version of a model artifact using its version ID) demonstrates how to leverage the versioning capability for rollback or historical analysis.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain46_10',
  NOW(),
  21,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_46_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_46_m_46_1_112',
  'A security team requires that access to a specific Amazon S3 bucket containing sensitive training data for Amazon Rekognition Custom Labels is restricted to only authorized IAM roles. Arrange the following steps to implement a bucket policy for this purpose.',
  'ordering',
  '["Identify the specific IAM roles that require access to the S3 bucket.","Create an S3 bucket policy that explicitly grants read-only access to the identified IAM roles for the bucket and its objects.","Attach the created S3 bucket policy to the target S3 bucket.","Test access from an unauthorized IAM role to ensure it is denied."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'The first step is to identify who needs access. Option A (Identify the specific IAM roles that require access to the S3 bucket) sets the scope for the policy. Next, Option B (Create an S3 bucket policy that explicitly grants read-only access to the identified IAM roles for the bucket and its objects) defines the actual permissions. Option C (Attach the created S3 bucket policy to the target S3 bucket) applies these rules to the bucket. Finally, Option D (Test access from an unauthorized IAM role to ensure it is denied) is a crucial verification step to confirm the policy is working as intended and enforcing least privilege.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain46_10',
  NOW(),
  22,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_46_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_46_m_46_1_113',
  'A company needs to ensure that all data transmitted to and from Amazon SageMaker inference endpoints is encrypted in transit using TLS. Arrange the following steps to configure secure inference endpoints.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create a SageMaker model from the trained model artifacts.","Create a SageMaker endpoint configuration, specifying the desired instance types and count.","Deploy the endpoint configuration to create a SageMaker endpoint.","Ensure client applications connect to the SageMaker endpoint using HTTPS."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'The process begins with defining the model itself. Option A (Create a SageMaker model from the trained model artifacts) is the first step. Next, Option B (Create a SageMaker endpoint configuration, specifying the desired instance types and count) defines the compute resources for the endpoint. Option C (Deploy the endpoint configuration to create a SageMaker endpoint) then provisions the actual endpoint. Finally, Option D (Ensure client applications connect to the SageMaker endpoint using HTTPS) is the crucial step to ensure encryption in transit, as SageMaker endpoints inherently support HTTPS for secure communication.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain46_10',
  NOW(),
  23,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_46_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_46_m_46_1_114',
  'A company is preparing to train a custom object detection model using Amazon Rekognition Custom Labels. They need to ensure their training images are securely stored and accessible. Arrange the following steps to prepare input data for Rekognition Custom Labels.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an Amazon S3 bucket for storing training images and manifest files.","Upload training images to the S3 bucket.","Create an Amazon Rekognition Custom Labels project.","Generate an Amazon S3 manifest file that lists the training images and their labels."]'::json,
  '{0,1,3,2}',
  'The initial step is to establish the storage location for the raw data. Option A (Create an Amazon S3 bucket for storing training images and manifest files) provides this. Then, Option B (Upload training images to the S3 bucket) populates the bucket with the actual data. Option D (Generate an Amazon S3 manifest file that lists the training images and their labels) creates the necessary metadata file that Rekognition uses to understand the dataset. Finally, Option C (Create an Amazon Rekognition Custom Labels project) sets up the project in Rekognition and links it to the prepared data.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain46_10',
  NOW(),
  24,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_46_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

