  NULL,
  'm_46_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_46_m_46_2_97',
  'A company wants to collect and process real-time application logs for anomaly detection using Amazon Kinesis Data Streams and AWS Lambda. Order the steps to implement this real-time ingestion and processing solution.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an Amazon Kinesis Data Stream.","Configure an AWS Lambda function to process records from the Kinesis stream.","Deploy a producer application to send logs to the Kinesis stream.","Set up IAM roles for Kinesis and Lambda for appropriate permissions."]'::json,
  '{0,3,2,1}',
  'Option A (Create an Amazon Kinesis Data Stream) is the first step to establish the streaming data channel. Next, Option D (Set up IAM roles) is essential to grant necessary permissions for services to interact with Kinesis and for Lambda to process data. Following this, Option C (Deploy a producer application) starts sending log data into the stream. Finally, Option B (Configure an AWS Lambda function) processes the incoming stream data for anomaly detection.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain46_10',
  NOW(),
  36,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_46_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_46_m_46_2_98',
  'A data pipeline needs to ingest data from multiple relational databases into a data lake on Amazon S3. Order the steps to use AWS Glue Data Catalog and AWS Glue ETL jobs for this batch ingestion.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create AWS Glue ETL jobs to extract data from databases, transform it, and load into S3.","Configure AWS Glue connections to the relational databases.","Define AWS Glue crawlers to discover schemas from the databases.","Run the AWS Glue ETL jobs on a schedule."]'::json,
  '{1,2,0,3}',
  'Option B (Configure AWS Glue connections) is the initial step to allow Glue to connect to the source databases. Next, Option C (Define AWS Glue crawlers) discovers the schema of the database tables and populates the Data Catalog. Following this, Option A (Create AWS Glue ETL jobs) defines the actual data extraction, transformation, and loading logic. Finally, Option D (Run the AWS Glue ETL jobs) executes the defined jobs, often on a schedule, to perform the ingestion.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain46_10',
  NOW(),
  37,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_46_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_46_m_46_2_99',
  'A retail company wants to implement real-time product recommendations using Amazon Personalize. Arrange the following steps to prepare and ingest interaction data for a Personalize solution.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an Amazon Personalize dataset group.","Prepare your historical user-item interaction data in CSV format, including user_id, item_id, and timestamp.","Create an interaction dataset within the dataset group.","Import the interaction data from Amazon S3 into the Personalize interaction dataset."]'::json,
  '{0,2,1,3}',
  'The first step in using Amazon Personalize is to create a container for your datasets. Option A (Create an Amazon Personalize dataset group) establishes this. Next, Option C (Create an interaction dataset within the dataset group) defines the schema for your interaction data. Before importing, the data must be in the correct format, so Option B (Prepare your historical user-item interaction data in CSV format, including user_id, item_id, and timestamp) ensures this. Finally, Option D (Import the interaction data from Amazon S3 into the Personalize interaction dataset) loads the prepared data into Personalize for model training.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain46_10',
  NOW(),
  38,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_46_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

