VALUES (
  'q_46_m_46_2_100',
  'An e-commerce platform needs to provide personalized product recommendations, which requires item metadata like category and brand. Arrange the following steps to prepare and ingest item data for Amazon Personalize.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an item dataset within the dataset group, defining the schema for item attributes.","Prepare your item metadata (e.g., item_id, category, brand) in CSV format.","Create an Amazon Personalize dataset group.","Import the item data from Amazon S3 into the Personalize item dataset."]'::json,
  '{2,0,1,3}',
  'The process begins with creating the top-level container for Personalize data. Option C (Create an Amazon Personalize dataset group) is the initial step. Then, Option A (Create an item dataset within the dataset group, defining the schema for item attributes) specifies the structure for the item data. Option B (Prepare your item metadata (e.g., item_id, category, brand) in CSV format) ensures the data conforms to this schema. Finally, Option D (Import the item data from Amazon S3 into the Personalize item dataset) loads the prepared data into Personalize.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain46_10',
  NOW(),
  39,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_46_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_46_m_46_2_101',
  'A business needs to forecast future product demand using Amazon Forecast. This requires historical time-series data. Arrange the following steps to provide training data for Amazon Forecast.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create a dataset group in Amazon Forecast.","Prepare your historical time-series data (e.g., timestamp, item_id, demand) in CSV format and upload to Amazon S3.","Create a target time series dataset within the dataset group, defining its schema.","Import the data from Amazon S3 into the target time series dataset."]'::json,
  '{0,2,1,3}',
  'The first step is to create the top-level container for your forecasting project. Option A (Create a dataset group in Amazon Forecast) initializes this. Next, Option C (Create a target time series dataset within the dataset group, defining its schema) defines the structure of the data Forecast will use. Option B (Prepare your historical time-series data (e.g., timestamp, item_id, demand) in CSV format and upload to Amazon S3) ensures the data is correctly formatted and available. Finally, Option D (Import the data from Amazon S3 into the target time series dataset) loads the data into Forecast for model training.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain46_10',
  NOW(),
  40,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_46_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_46_m_46_2_102',
  'A data engineering team needs to prepare a large dataset for offline inference using Amazon SageMaker Batch Transform. Arrange the following steps to prepare the input data for a Batch Transform job.',
  'ordering',
  '["Upload the input data files (e.g., CSV, JSON) to an Amazon S3 bucket.","Ensure the input data format matches the expectations of the SageMaker model.","Create a SageMaker model from a trained model artifact.","Configure and start a SageMaker Batch Transform job, specifying the S3 input location and model name."]'::json,
  '{2,1,0,3}',
  'Before running a Batch Transform job, a model must exist. Option C (Create a SageMaker model from a trained model artifact) is the first step. Next, the input data must be compatible with this model, so Option B (Ensure the input data format matches the expectations of the SageMaker model) is critical. Option A (Upload the input data files (e.g., CSV, JSON) to an Amazon S3 bucket) makes the data accessible. Finally, Option D (Configure and start a SageMaker Batch Transform job, specifying the S3 input location and model name) initiates the inference process.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain46_10',
  NOW(),
  41,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_46_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

