VALUES (
  'q_46_m_46_2_103',
  'A content moderation team wants to use Amazon Comprehend to automatically classify user-generated content. They need to train a custom classification model. Arrange the following steps to prepare and upload data for Amazon Comprehend custom classification.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create a CSV file containing text and corresponding labels for each document.","Upload the CSV training file to an Amazon S3 bucket.","Create a Comprehend custom classifier, specifying the S3 input location and document format.","Define the set of custom labels for your classification task."]'::json,
  '{3,0,1,2}',
  'The first step in custom classification is to define what you want to classify. Option D (Define the set of custom labels for your classification task) establishes the categories. Next, Option A (Create a CSV file containing text and corresponding labels for each document) formats your data according to these labels. Option B (Upload the CSV training file to an Amazon S3 bucket) makes this data accessible to Comprehend. Finally, Option C (Create a Comprehend custom classifier, specifying the S3 input location and document format) initiates the training of the custom model.',
