INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_46_m_46_3_98',
  'After successfully training a new machine learning model, an MLOps team needs to register it in Amazon SageMaker Model Registry for versioning and approval workflows. Arrange the following steps to register a model in SageMaker Model Registry.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create a model package group in SageMaker Model Registry.","Define the model artifacts'' S3 location and inference container image.","Create a model package version within the model package group, referencing the model artifacts.","Approve the model package version for deployment."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'The first step is to create a logical grouping for model versions. Option A (Create a model package group in SageMaker Model Registry) serves this purpose. Before registering, the model''s components must be defined, so Option B (Define the model artifacts'' S3 location and inference container image) specifies where the model lives and how it runs. Option C (Create a model package version within the model package group, referencing the model artifacts) then registers a specific version of the model. Finally, Option D (Approve the model package version for deployment) marks the model as ready for production use, often after manual review.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain46_10',
  NOW(),
  64,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_46_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_46_m_46_3_99',
  'To conduct A/B testing for different model versions, an MLOps team wants to deploy multiple production variants to a single Amazon SageMaker endpoint. Arrange the following steps to create a SageMaker endpoint with multiple production variants.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create two or more SageMaker models, each representing a different model version.","Create a SageMaker endpoint configuration, defining multiple production variants with different model names and traffic weights.","Deploy the endpoint configuration to create the SageMaker endpoint.","Direct inference requests to the endpoint, allowing SageMaker to route traffic based on weights."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'The first step is to have the different models ready for deployment. Option A (Create two or more SageMaker models, each representing a different model version) provides these. Next, Option B (Create a SageMaker endpoint configuration, defining multiple production variants with different model names and traffic weights) specifies how these models will be hosted and how traffic will be split. Option C (Deploy the endpoint configuration to create the SageMaker endpoint) provisions the actual endpoint with these variants. Finally, Option D (Direct inference requests to the endpoint, allowing SageMaker to route traffic based on weights) utilizes the A/B testing setup.',
