  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (Consistency of predictions across similar inputs) is a key indicator of reliability, ensuring the model behaves predictably. Option B (Robustness to noisy or slightly perturbed data) is also crucial, as real-world data often contains imperfections, and a reliable model should not drastically change its predictions. Option C (The specific brand of GPU used for training) is a hardware detail, not a model reliability aspect. Option D (The number of lines of code in the model) is a measure of code complexity, not model reliability. Option E (The amount of RAM available on the inference endpoint) relates to deployment infrastructure, not the inherent reliability of the model itself.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain48_10',
  NOW(),
  7,
  NULL,
