INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_48_m_48_5_64',
  'A data science team needs to evaluate a classification model where the cost of false negatives (e.g., failing to detect a critical system failure) is significantly higher than false positives. Which evaluation metrics should they prioritize? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Recall","F1-Score","Accuracy","Precision","Area Under the Curve (AUC)"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'When false negatives are costly, the model''s ability to identify all positive cases is paramount. Recall (Option A) directly measures this, quantifying the proportion of actual positives that were correctly identified. F1-Score (Option B) is also highly relevant as it provides a harmonic mean of precision and recall, offering a balanced view, especially useful when both false positives and false negatives have consequences. Accuracy (Option C) can be misleading with imbalanced classes. Precision (Option D) focuses on minimizing false positives, which is not the primary concern here. AUC (Option E) provides an overall measure but doesn''t specifically prioritize minimizing false negatives.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain48_10',
  NOW(),
  12,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_48_5',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_48_m_48_5_65',
  'A machine learning engineer wants to compare two different recommendation models in production to see which one drives more user engagement. Which evaluation strategies are suitable for this goal? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["A/B Testing","Online Evaluation","Offline Evaluation","K-fold Cross-validation","Holdout Validation"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'To compare models in production with real user engagement, A/B Testing (Option A) is ideal as it directs live traffic to different model versions and measures their direct impact. Online Evaluation (Option B) is a broader term that encompasses A/B testing and other methods of assessing model performance in a live environment. Offline Evaluation (Option C), K-fold Cross-validation (Option D), and Holdout Validation (Option E) are techniques used during model development and training, not for direct comparison in a production environment with live user interaction.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain48_10',
  NOW(),
  13,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_48_5',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_48_m_48_5_66',
  'For evaluating a regression model, which metrics are commonly used to quantify the prediction error and assess the model''s fit to the data? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Mean Squared Error (MSE)","R-squared","Accuracy","F1-Score","Area Under the Curve (AUC)"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Mean Squared Error (MSE) (Option A) is a standard metric for regression models, measuring the average of the squares of the errors. R-squared (Option B), also known as the coefficient of determination, indicates the proportion of the variance in the dependent variable that is predictable from the independent variables. Accuracy (Option C), F1-Score (Option D), and Area Under the Curve (AUC) (Option E) are metrics used for classification models, not regression.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain48_10',
  NOW(),
  14,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_48_5',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_48_m_48_5_67',
  'A large e-commerce company has developed a new recommendation engine for its product catalog, aiming to improve customer engagement and conversion rates. Before a full rollout, the data science team needs to rigorously evaluate the model''s performance and impact in a production-like environment. They are particularly concerned with both the model''s predictive accuracy and its real-world effect on user behavior. Which of the following evaluation strategies are most appropriate for assessing both the offline performance and the real-world business impact of this new recommendation engine? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Calculating the Area Under the Receiver Operating Characteristic (AUC-ROC) curve on a holdout dataset.","Performing an A/B test by deploying the new model to a subset of users and comparing their engagement metrics against a control group.","Analyzing the model''s confusion matrix to understand its false positive and false negative rates for product recommendations.","Monitoring the model''s training loss and validation loss over several epochs to detect overfitting during development.","Computing the Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE) on the predicted product ratings against actual user ratings in a test set."]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (correct) is appropriate for assessing the offline predictive accuracy of a recommendation system, especially if the problem is framed as a binary classification (e.g., predicting whether a user will click or purchase an item). AUC-ROC provides a robust measure of a classifier''s performance across various thresholds. Option B (correct) is essential for evaluating the real-world business impact of the recommendation engine. An A/B test allows the team to measure actual changes in user engagement, conversion rates, and other key performance indicators when exposed to the new model versus a control group. Option C is a detailed offline metric for classification but AUC-ROC provides a more aggregate view of performance. Option D is a technique for monitoring training progress and detecting overfitting during model development, not for evaluating the final model''s performance or business impact. Option E would be suitable if the recommendation engine were predicting continuous ratings (a regression problem), but for engagement and conversion, classification metrics like AUC-ROC are often more relevant.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain48_10',
  NOW(),
  15,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_48_5',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

