  '{0,1}',
  'Classification (Option A) and Regression (Option B) are both types of supervised learning problems, which inherently require labeled historical data. In classification, the labels are discrete categories, while in regression, they are continuous numerical values. Clustering (Option C), Dimensionality Reduction (Option D), and Anomaly Detection (Option E) are typically unsupervised learning tasks that do not require labeled data for training.',
