  '{0,1}',
  'Predicting customer churn (Option A) is a binary classification problem (churn/no churn). Identifying fraudulent transactions (Option B) is also a binary classification problem (fraud/not fraud). Forecasting product demand (Option C) and estimating product price (Option E) are regression tasks. Recommending the next best item (Option D) is typically a recommendation system problem, which can involve classification but is often framed differently.',
