  'The first step is to load the dataset into the analysis environment (Option B). Next, the specific numerical feature for which the box plot is desired must be selected (Option C). A box plot is then generated for the chosen feature (Option D). Finally, the box plot is interpreted to understand the data''s central tendency (median), spread (quartiles), and identify any outliers (Option A).',
