  'Order the general steps a data scientist would follow to diagnose common data quality issues in a newly acquired dataset.',
  'ordering',
  '["Summarize missing values, duplicates, and inconsistent entries.","Inspect data types and schema for correctness.","Profile the dataset to understand its structure and content.","Identify outliers and anomalies through statistical methods and visualizations."]'::json,
  '{2,1,0,3}',
  'Diagnosing data quality issues typically begins with profiling the dataset to get a high-level overview of its structure and content (Option C). Following this, the data types and schema are inspected to ensure they are correct and consistent with expectations (Option B). Next, a detailed summary of missing values, duplicate records, and inconsistent entries is generated (Option A). Finally, statistical methods and visualizations are used to identify outliers and anomalies that might impact model performance (Option D).',
