  'A data scientist is preparing text data for a natural language processing (NLP) model. Order the typical feature engineering steps for text tokenization.',
  'ordering',
  '["Convert text to lowercase.","Split text into individual words or subword units.","Remove punctuation and special characters.","Apply stemming or lemmatization."]'::json,
  '{0,2,1,3}',
  'Before tokenization, it''s common practice to convert all text to lowercase to standardize words and reduce vocabulary size (Option A). Next, punctuation and special characters are typically removed to clean the text (Option C). The cleaned text is then split into individual tokens (words or subword units) (Option B). Finally, stemming or lemmatization can be applied to reduce words to their base forms, further standardizing the tokens (Option D).',
