  NULL,
  'm_47_1',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_47_m_47_1_86',
  'When preparing data for a deep learning model, it''s common to convert categorical features into numerical embeddings. Order the steps for creating feature embeddings.',
  'ordering',
  '["Train a neural network to learn the embeddings.","Map unique categories to integer IDs.","Define the embedding layer size.","Identify the categorical feature for embedding."]'::json,
  '{3,1,2,0}',
  'The process starts by identifying the specific categorical feature that will be converted into embeddings (Option D). Each unique category within this feature is then mapped to a distinct integer ID (Option B). The size of the embedding layer, which determines the dimensionality of the learned embeddings, is defined (Option C). Finally, a neural network is trained, often as part of a larger model, to learn the optimal numerical representations (embeddings) for each integer ID (Option A).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain47_10',
  NOW(),
  48,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_47_1',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_47_m_47_1_87',
  'A data engineer needs to ensure data consistency across multiple sources before merging them for model training. Order the general steps to achieve data consistency.',
  'ordering',
  '["Standardize data formats and units.","Identify inconsistencies across data sources.","Merge the consistent datasets.","Define data quality rules and standards."]'::json,
  '{3,1,0,2}',
  'The first step in ensuring data consistency is to define clear data quality rules and standards that all data should adhere to (Option D). Next, the datasets are analyzed to identify specific inconsistencies, such as differing formats, units, or conflicting values, across the various sources (Option B). Once inconsistencies are identified, data formats and units are standardized to align with the defined rules (Option A). Finally, the now consistent datasets can be reliably merged for model training (Option C).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain47_10',
  NOW(),
  49,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_47_1',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_47_m_47_1_88',
  'To reduce noise in a numerical feature, a data scientist decides to apply a smoothing technique. Order the general steps for smoothing a time series feature using a moving average.',
  'ordering',
  '["Calculate the average of values within a defined window.","Identify the time series feature.","Replace original values with the calculated moving averages.","Define the window size for the moving average."]'::json,
  '{1,3,0,2}',
  'First, the specific time series feature that requires smoothing is identified (Option B). Next, the window size for the moving average, which determines how many previous data points are included in each average calculation, is defined (Option D). The average of values within this defined window is then calculated sequentially across the time series (Option A). Finally, the original values in the feature are replaced with their corresponding calculated moving averages, resulting in a smoothed series (Option C).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain47_10',
  NOW(),
  50,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_47_1',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_47_m_47_1_89',
  'A data scientist is preparing a dataset with missing numerical values and decides to use imputation. Order the steps to handle missing data using a common imputation strategy like mean or median imputation.',
  'ordering',
  '["Identify the numerical features that contain missing values.","Calculate the mean or median of the non-missing values for each identified feature.","Replace the missing values in each feature with its calculated mean or median.","Verify that all missing values have been addressed."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'To handle missing numerical data using imputation, the first step is to identify the specific numerical features that contain missing values (Option A). For each of these features, the mean or median of its existing (non-missing) values is calculated (Option B). Then, the missing values within each feature are replaced with its corresponding calculated mean or median (Option C). Finally, it''s important to verify that all missing values have been successfully addressed, often by re-checking for nulls (Option D).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain47_10',
  NOW(),
  51,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_47_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_47_m_47_1_90',
  'A machine learning engineer needs to normalize numerical features in a dataset to a standard range (e.g., 0 to 1) before training a neural network. Order the steps to perform min-max scaling.',
  'ordering',
  '["Apply the calculated scaling transformation to the feature, mapping values to the new range.","Identify the numerical feature(s) to be normalized.","Calculate the minimum and maximum values of each identified feature.","Store the scaling parameters (min and max) for future use on new data."]'::json,
  '{1,2,0,3}',
  'To perform min-max scaling, the process begins by identifying the numerical feature(s) that require normalization (Option B). For each identified feature, its minimum and maximum values are calculated (Option C). The calculated scaling transformation (using these min and max values) is then applied to the feature, mapping all its values to the desired range, typically 0 to 1 (Option A). Finally, it''s crucial to store these scaling parameters (the original min and max) so that the same transformation can be consistently applied to new, unseen data during inference (Option D).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain47_10',
  NOW(),
  52,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_47_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_47_m_47_1_91',
  'An NLP specialist is cleaning text data to improve the performance of a sentiment analysis model. Order the steps to effectively remove common stop words from a text corpus.',
  'ordering',
  '["Load a predefined list of stop words (e.g., ''the'', ''is'', ''a'').","Iterate through each document or sentence in the text corpus.","For each document, remove words that are present in the stop word list.","Tokenize the text into individual words if not already done."]'::json,
  '{0,3,1,2}',
  'To effectively remove stop words, the first step is to load or define a list of common stop words (Option A). If the text is not already tokenized, it must be broken down into individual words (Option D). Then, the process involves iterating through each document or sentence in the text corpus (Option B). For each word in a document, it is checked against the loaded stop word list, and if a match is found, the word is removed (Option C). This ensures that common, less informative words do not unduly influence the model.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain47_10',
  NOW(),
  53,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_47_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_47_m_47_1_92',
  'A company needs to label a large dataset of images for a new object detection model using human annotators. Order the steps to leverage Amazon Mechanical Turk for this data labeling task.',
  'ordering',
  '["Design and create a Human Intelligence Task (HIT) that specifies labeling instructions and output format.","Upload the unlabeled image data to an Amazon S3 bucket.","Publish the HITs on Amazon Mechanical Turk and manage worker qualifications.","Retrieve the labeled data from S3 and perform quality control checks."]'::json,
  '{1,0,2,3}',
  'Leveraging Amazon Mechanical Turk for data labeling starts with uploading the unlabeled image data to an Amazon S3 bucket, making it accessible for the labeling process (Option B). Next, a Human Intelligence Task (HIT) is designed, which includes clear labeling instructions, examples, and defines the expected output format for the annotators (Option A). These HITs are then published on Amazon Mechanical Turk, and worker qualifications are managed to ensure quality (Option C). Finally, after workers complete the tasks, the labeled data is retrieved from S3, and quality control checks are performed to validate the annotations (Option D).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain47_10',
  NOW(),
  54,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_47_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_47_m_47_1_93',
  'A machine learning engineer is working with a limited image dataset and needs to augment it to improve model generalization. Order the steps to apply common image augmentation techniques.',
  'ordering',
  '["Apply various transformations (e.g., rotation, flipping, zooming, brightness changes) to the original images.","Load the original image dataset into the processing environment.","Generate new augmented images, increasing the dataset size.","Store the augmented dataset for model training."]'::json,
  '{1,0,2,3}',
  'To augment an image dataset, the first step is to load the original image dataset into the processing environment (Option B). Then, various transformations such as rotation, horizontal flipping, zooming, or brightness adjustments are applied to these original images (Option A). These transformations generate new, augmented images, effectively increasing the size and diversity of the dataset without collecting new data (Option C). Finally, the combined original and augmented dataset is stored, ready for use in model training to enhance generalization (Option D).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain47_10',
  NOW(),
  55,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_47_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_47_m_47_1_94',
  'A machine learning team is preparing a dataset for model training and needs to ensure data quality and consistency across various sources. Order the general steps to achieve this.',
  'ordering',
  '["Define a data validation schema and rules for data types, ranges, and formats.","Identify and consolidate data from all relevant sources into a central location.","Implement automated checks to flag or correct data that violates the defined rules.","Cleanse and transform the data to resolve inconsistencies, missing values, and errors."]'::json,
  '{1,0,3,2}',
  'Ensuring data quality and consistency begins with identifying and consolidating data from all relevant sources into a central location, such as an Amazon S3 bucket or a data lake (Option B). Next, a comprehensive data validation schema and rules are defined, specifying expected data types, acceptable ranges, and formats (Option A). The data is then cleansed and transformed to resolve any inconsistencies, missing values, or errors identified during initial profiling (Option D). Finally, automated checks are implemented to continuously flag or correct any incoming data that violates the defined quality rules, maintaining consistency over time (Option C).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain47_10',
  NOW(),
  56,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_47_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_47_m_47_1_95',
  'A data scientist is preparing categorical features for a deep learning model and decides to use embeddings. Order the steps to convert high-cardinality categorical features into numerical embeddings.',
  'ordering',
  '["Train an embedding layer as part of the deep learning model or pre-train it separately.","Map each unique category to a unique integer ID.","Identify high-cardinality categorical features in the dataset.","Replace the original categorical feature with the learned numerical embedding vectors."]'::json,
  '{2,1,0,3}',
  'Converting high-cardinality categorical features into numerical embeddings starts by identifying these features in the dataset (Option C). Each unique category within these features is then mapped to a unique integer ID, which serves as input to the embedding layer (Option B). An embedding layer is then trained, either as an integral part of the main deep learning model or pre-trained separately, to learn dense numerical representations for each integer ID (Option A). Finally, the original categorical feature is replaced with these learned numerical embedding vectors, which capture semantic relationships and are suitable for deep learning models (Option D).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain47_10',
  NOW(),
  57,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_47_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_47_m_47_1_96',
  'A healthcare analytics company is preparing a large dataset of patient health records for a predictive model. The dataset, stored in Amazon S3, contains numerous missing values in critical columns like ''BloodPressure'' and ''MedicationDosage''. Imputing these missing values is crucial to prevent data loss and ensure model accuracy. The data science team decides to use a sophisticated imputation strategy, such as mean or median imputation, based on the feature distribution. Order the steps to handle missing data effectively using Amazon SageMaker.',
  'ordering',
  '["Store the raw patient health records with missing values in Amazon S3.","Identify columns with missing values and determine an appropriate imputation strategy for each.","Implement and execute a SageMaker processing job to apply the chosen imputation strategy.","Verify the imputed dataset to ensure missing values have been correctly handled."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'The process begins with data storage. Option A (Store the raw patient health records with missing values in Amazon S3) makes the raw data available. Next, Option B (Identify columns with missing values and determine an appropriate imputation strategy for each) is a critical analytical step to understand the extent and nature of missingness. Following this, Option C (Implement and execute a SageMaker processing job to apply the chosen imputation strategy) performs the actual imputation in a scalable environment. Finally, Option D (Verify the imputed dataset to ensure missing values have been correctly handled) is essential for data quality assurance before model training.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain47_10',
  NOW(),
  58,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_47_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_47_m_47_1_97',
  'An autonomous driving research team is collecting vast amounts of sensor data, including LiDAR and camera feeds, to train perception models. The raw data is stored in Amazon S3. To improve the robustness and generalization of their models, they need to apply data augmentation techniques like rotations, flips, and brightness adjustments to their image datasets. This process must be scalable and integrated into their ML pipeline. Order the steps to perform data augmentation for image datasets using AWS services.',
  'ordering',
  '["Store the raw image datasets in an Amazon S3 bucket.","Define the specific augmentation transformations (e.g., rotation angles, flip types, brightness ranges).","Implement and execute a SageMaker processing job to apply the defined augmentation techniques to the images.","Verify the augmented dataset in S3 for diversity and quality."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'The initial step is data storage. Option A (Store the raw image datasets in an Amazon S3 bucket) ensures the raw data is accessible. Next, Option B (Define the specific augmentation transformations (e.g., rotation angles, flip types, brightness ranges)) is the design phase where the augmentation strategy is formulated. Following this, Option C (Implement and execute a SageMaker processing job to apply the defined augmentation techniques to the images) performs the actual augmentation in a scalable environment. Finally, Option D (Verify the augmented dataset in S3 for diversity and quality) is crucial for ensuring the effectiveness of the augmentation and the quality of the new data.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain47_10',
  NOW(),
  59,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_47_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_47_m_47_1_98',
  'A retail company is building a product recommendation system and needs to label a large dataset of product images with specific categories (e.g., ''shirt'', ''pants'', ''shoes''). They have millions of unlabelled images stored in Amazon S3. To efficiently and accurately label this data at scale, they decide to use Amazon SageMaker Ground Truth. Order the steps to set up and execute a data labeling job using Amazon SageMaker Ground Truth.',
  'ordering',
  '["Store the unlabelled product images in an Amazon S3 bucket.","Create a SageMaker Ground Truth labeling job, specifying input S3 location, output S3 location, and labeling instructions.","Monitor the labeling job progress and review labeled data for quality control.","Define the label categories and task type (e.g., image classification, bounding box)."]'::json,
  '{0,3,1,2}',
  'The process begins with data storage. Option A (Store the unlabelled product images in an Amazon S3 bucket) makes the raw data available for labeling. Next, Option D (Define the label categories and task type (e.g., image classification, bounding box)) is a crucial design step to specify what needs to be labeled and how. Following this, Option B (Create a SageMaker Ground Truth labeling job, specifying input S3 location, output S3 location, and labeling instructions) configures and launches the labeling workflow. Finally, Option C (Monitor the labeling job progress and review labeled data for quality control) is essential for ensuring the accuracy and consistency of the human-generated labels.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain47_10',
  NOW(),
  60,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_47_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_47_m_47_1_99',
  'A financial services company is developing a machine learning model to detect fraudulent transactions. Their dataset contains various numerical features, such as transaction amount and frequency, which have widely different scales. To prevent features with larger numerical values from dominating the model training process, the data science team needs to normalize these features (e.g., using Min-Max scaling or Z-score standardization). Order the steps to normalize numerical features using Amazon SageMaker.',
  'ordering',
  '["Store the raw transaction data with varying numerical scales in Amazon S3.","Identify the numerical features that require normalization.","Implement and execute a SageMaker processing job to apply the chosen normalization technique.","Verify the normalized dataset to ensure features are within the desired range or distribution."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'The initial step is data storage. Option A (Store the raw transaction data with varying numerical scales in Amazon S3) ensures the raw data is accessible. Next, Option B (Identify the numerical features that require normalization) is a necessary analytical step to pinpoint which features need scaling. Following this, Option C (Implement and execute a SageMaker processing job to apply the chosen normalization technique) performs the actual scaling in a scalable environment. Finally, Option D (Verify the normalized dataset to ensure features are within the desired range or distribution) is crucial for data quality assurance before model training.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain47_10',
  NOW(),
  61,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_47_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_47_m_47_1_100',
  'A social media analytics company is building a model to categorize user comments. The raw comments are stored as text in Amazon S3. Before converting these comments into numerical representations (embeddings) for the model, the team needs to preprocess the text by removing common, non-informative words (stop words) to reduce noise and improve model focus. Order the steps to effectively remove stop words from text data using Amazon SageMaker.',
  'ordering',
  '["Store the raw user comments in an Amazon S3 bucket.","Define a list of stop words relevant to the language and domain of the comments.","Implement and execute a SageMaker processing job to remove the identified stop words from the text.","Verify the processed text to ensure stop words have been successfully removed."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'The process begins with data storage. Option A (Store the raw user comments in an Amazon S3 bucket) makes the raw text data available. Next, Option B (Define a list of stop words relevant to the language and domain of the comments) is a crucial analytical step to identify the words to be removed. Following this, Option C (Implement and execute a SageMaker processing job to remove the identified stop words from the text) performs the actual text cleaning in a scalable environment. Finally, Option D (Verify the processed text to ensure stop words have been successfully removed) is essential for data quality assurance before further processing.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain47_10',
  NOW(),
  62,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_47_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_47_m_47_1_101',
  'An online content platform is developing a content recommendation model. They have a large corpus of article text stored in Amazon S3. To represent these articles numerically for machine learning, they plan to generate text embeddings (e.g., using a pre-trained BERT model or training a custom Word2Vec model). This requires specific preprocessing steps before the embedding generation. Order the steps to prepare text data for embeddings using Amazon SageMaker.',
  'ordering',
  '["Store the raw article text corpus in an Amazon S3 bucket.","Perform text cleaning, including lowercasing, punctuation removal, and potentially stop word removal.","Tokenize the cleaned text into individual words or subword units.","Generate text embeddings (e.g., using a pre-trained model or training a custom one) on the tokenized text."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'The initial step is data storage. Option A (Store the raw article text corpus in an Amazon S3 bucket) ensures the raw text is accessible. Next, Option B (Perform text cleaning, including lowercasing, punctuation removal, and potentially stop word removal) standardizes the text and removes noise. Following this, Option C (Tokenize the cleaned text into individual words or subword units) breaks down the text into discrete units suitable for embedding models. Finally, Option D (Generate text embeddings (e.g., using a pre-trained model or training a custom one) on the tokenized text) converts the text into numerical vector representations.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain47_10',
  NOW(),
  63,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_47_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_47_m_47_1_102',
  'A medical imaging startup is building a diagnostic model for rare diseases using image data. Due to the rarity of the diseases, they have a highly imbalanced dataset where positive cases are significantly fewer than negative cases. This imbalance can lead to models that perform poorly on the minority class. The data science team decides to mitigate this by oversampling the minority class using techniques like SMOTE. Order the steps to mitigate class imbalance in a dataset using Amazon SageMaker.',
  'ordering',
  '["Store the imbalanced medical image dataset in an Amazon S3 bucket.","Identify the minority and majority classes and quantify the class imbalance ratio.","Implement and execute a SageMaker processing job to apply oversampling (e.g., SMOTE) or undersampling techniques.","Verify the class distribution in the new dataset to confirm balance has improved."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'The process begins with data storage. Option A (Store the imbalanced medical image dataset in an Amazon S3 bucket) makes the raw data available. Next, Option B (Identify the minority and majority classes and quantify the class imbalance ratio) is a critical analytical step to understand the problem. Following this, Option C (Implement and execute a SageMaker processing job to apply oversampling (e.g., SMOTE) or undersampling techniques) performs the actual rebalancing of the dataset. Finally, Option D (Verify the class distribution in the new dataset to confirm balance has improved) is essential to confirm the effectiveness of the mitigation strategy.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain47_10',
  NOW(),
  64,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_47_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

