  NULL,
  'Amazon Athena (Option A in left) is a serverless interactive query service that allows running standard SQL queries directly on data stored in Amazon S3, making it ideal for initial data exploration and ad-hoc analysis. AWS Glue (Option B in left) is a serverless extract, transform, and load (ETL) service that can catalog data, discover schemas, and perform complex data transformations, making it suitable for preparing data for ML. Amazon SageMaker Processing (Option C in left) provides managed compute infrastructure for running large-scale data processing jobs, including feature engineering and data validation, which are critical steps before training an ML model.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain47_10',
  NOW(),
  23,
  '{"left":["Amazon Athena","AWS Glue","Amazon SageMaker Processing"],"right":["Interactive SQL queries on S3 data","Serverless ETL service for data cataloging and transformation","Managed compute for large-scale data processing jobs"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
