  'Option B (correct) Amazon SageMaker is a fully managed service that provides every developer and data scientist with the ability to build, train, and deploy machine learning models quickly. It abstracts away the infrastructure management. Option A (incorrect) Amazon EC2 provides virtual servers but requires manual infrastructure management. Option C (incorrect) AWS Lambda is a serverless compute service for running code, not specifically for the end-to-end ML lifecycle. Option D (incorrect) Amazon S3 is an object storage service.',
