  NOW(),
  93,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_49_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_49_m_49_2_43',
  'A media company wants to create dynamic, lifelike voiceovers for its articles and videos in multiple languages. The solution needs to be highly scalable, support a wide range of voices and speaking styles, and integrate seamlessly with existing content management systems. The company aims to minimize the development effort and operational overhead. Which AWS service is best suited for this requirement?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon Transcribe","Amazon Polly","Amazon Lex","Amazon Comprehend"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is Amazon Polly, a text-to-speech service that turns text into lifelike speech. It supports multiple languages and a wide selection of voices and speaking styles, making it ideal for creating dynamic voiceovers for articles and videos. It is a fully managed service, minimizing development effort and operational overhead.
Option A (incorrect) is Amazon Transcribe, which is a speech-to-text service used to convert audio into text, the opposite of what is required.
Option C (incorrect) is Amazon Lex, a service for building conversational interfaces (chatbots, voicebots) using voice and text, not for generating voiceovers from text.
Option D (incorrect) is Amazon Comprehend, a natural language processing (NLP) service that uncovers insights and relationships in text, not for text-to-speech conversion.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain49_10',
  NOW(),
  94,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_49_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_49_m_49_2_44',
  'A customer support center wants to automate responses to common customer inquiries via a chatbot. The chatbot needs to understand natural language, engage in multi-turn conversations, and integrate with backend systems to retrieve customer-specific information. The company wants a fully managed service that minimizes development time and scales automatically with demand. Which AWS service should be recommended to build this conversational AI interface?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon Rekognition","Amazon Polly","Amazon Lex","Amazon Transcribe"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is Amazon Lex, a service for building conversational interfaces (chatbots and voicebots) into any application using voice and text. It provides advanced deep learning functionalities for automatic speech recognition (ASR) to convert speech to text, and natural language understanding (NLU) to recognize the intent of the text, enabling multi-turn conversations and integration with backend systems. It is fully managed and scales automatically, meeting the requirements.
Option A (incorrect) is Amazon Rekognition, an image and video analysis service, not for building chatbots.
Option B (incorrect) is Amazon Polly, a text-to-speech service, which could be used as a component for voice output but is not the primary service for building the conversational interface itself.
Option D (incorrect) is Amazon Transcribe, a speech-to-text service, which could be used as a component for voice input but is not the primary service for building the conversational interface itself.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain49_10',
  NOW(),
  95,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_49_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_49_m_49_2_45',
  'A large enterprise wants to build a custom machine learning model for a highly specialized task, such as predicting equipment failures based on proprietary sensor data. The data scientists require fine-grained control over the training environment, including custom algorithms, specific framework versions (e.g., a particular TensorFlow version not directly supported by SageMaker''s built-in algorithms), and access to advanced debugging tools. The company also needs to manage the entire ML lifecycle, from data preparation to deployment, within a unified platform. Which AWS service is best suited for building and managing this custom ML solution?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon Comprehend","Amazon Rekognition","Amazon SageMaker","Amazon Polly"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is Amazon SageMaker. It is a fully managed service that provides every developer and data scientist with the ability to build, train, and deploy machine learning models quickly. It offers the flexibility to use custom algorithms, specific framework versions (via custom containers), and provides tools for data preparation, training, debugging (SageMaker Debugger), and deployment. This level of control and comprehensive lifecycle management makes it ideal for highly specialized custom ML solutions.
Option A (incorrect) is Amazon Comprehend, a natural language processing (NLP) service for text analysis, not for building custom ML models from scratch.
Option B (incorrect) is Amazon Rekognition, an image and video analysis service, not for building custom ML models.
Option D (incorrect) is Amazon Polly, a text-to-speech service, which is not relevant for building custom ML models.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain49_10',
  NOW(),
  96,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_49_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_49_m_49_2_46',
  'A research institution is processing vast archives of historical documents, including scanned images of handwritten notes and printed texts. They need to extract specific entities (e.g., names, dates, organizations) and key phrases from these documents to build a knowledge graph. The institution requires a scalable, serverless solution that can handle large volumes of text and accurately identify relevant information without requiring custom model training. Which AWS service is best suited for this natural language processing (NLP) task?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon Transcribe","Amazon Textract","Amazon Comprehend","Amazon Lex"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is Amazon Comprehend, a natural language processing (NLP) service that uses machine learning to find insights and relationships in text. It can identify entities (people, places, brands, events), key phrases, language, sentiments, and other text attributes without requiring custom model training. This makes it ideal for extracting specific information from large volumes of documents. While Amazon Textract (Option B) can extract text from scanned documents, Comprehend is specifically for understanding the content of that text.
Option A (incorrect) is Amazon Transcribe, a speech-to-text service, not for text analysis.
Option B (incorrect) is Amazon Textract, which extracts text and data from scanned documents, but does not perform the NLP analysis to identify entities and key phrases from the extracted text itself. It would be a prerequisite step, but not the service for the core NLP task.
Option D (incorrect) is Amazon Lex, a service for building conversational interfaces, not for text analysis of documents.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain49_10',
  NOW(),
  97,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_49_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_49_m_49_2_47',
  'A large media company has an extensive library of video content. They want to automatically detect objects, scenes, activities, and inappropriate content within these videos for content tagging, searchability, and moderation purposes. The solution needs to be highly scalable, cost-effective, and require no machine learning expertise to implement. Which AWS service should be recommended for this video analysis task?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon Polly","Amazon Transcribe","Amazon Rekognition","Amazon SageMaker"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is Amazon Rekognition, a service that makes it easy to add image and video analysis to your applications. It can detect objects, scenes, activities, celebrities, and inappropriate content in images and videos. It is fully managed, scalable, and requires no ML expertise, perfectly matching the company''s requirements for automated video content analysis.
Option A (incorrect) is Amazon Polly, a text-to-speech service.
Option B (incorrect) is Amazon Transcribe, a speech-to-text service.
Option D (incorrect) is Amazon SageMaker, which is used for building, training, and deploying custom ML models, requiring ML expertise, and is not a pre-trained service for general image and video analysis.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain49_10',
  NOW(),
  98,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_49_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_49_m_49_2_48',
  'A call center needs to analyze customer service calls to identify common issues, agent performance, and sentiment. The audio recordings of these calls are stored in Amazon S3. The company requires a solution that can accurately convert the spoken words into text, identify different speakers, and provide timestamps for each word, enabling further downstream analysis. The solution must be scalable and handle various audio formats. Which AWS service is best suited for converting these audio recordings into text?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon Lex","Amazon Polly","Amazon Transcribe","Amazon Comprehend"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is Amazon Transcribe, a fully managed speech-to-text service. It can accurately convert audio recordings into text, identify different speakers (speaker diarization), and provide timestamps for each word. It supports various audio formats and is highly scalable, making it ideal for analyzing call center recordings.
Option A (incorrect) is Amazon Lex, a service for building conversational interfaces, not for transcribing audio.
Option B (incorrect) is Amazon Polly, a text-to-speech service, which performs the opposite function of what is required.
Option D (incorrect) is Amazon Comprehend, a natural language processing service that analyzes text, but it does not convert audio to text.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain49_10',
  NOW(),
  99,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_49_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_49_m_49_2_49',
  'A startup is developing a new mobile application that requires a personalized recommendation system. They want to leverage AWS machine learning services but have limited ML expertise and a tight budget. The recommendation system needs to provide real-time recommendations based on user behavior and item attributes. Which AWS service is specifically designed to build, train, and deploy recommendation models without requiring deep ML knowledge, while being cost-effective for a startup?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon SageMaker","Amazon Personalize","Amazon Rekognition","Amazon Comprehend"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is Amazon Personalize, a fully managed machine learning service that makes it easy for developers to create personalized recommendations for their customers. It uses the same machine learning technology as Amazon.com for recommendations, requiring no prior ML experience. It handles data processing, model training, and deployment, making it ideal for startups with limited ML expertise and a need for cost-effective, real-time recommendations.
Option A (incorrect) is Amazon SageMaker, which is a powerful service for building, training, and deploying custom ML models. While it offers immense flexibility, it typically requires more ML expertise and active management compared to Amazon Personalize for a specific task like recommendations.
Option C (incorrect) is Amazon Rekognition, an image and video analysis service, not for recommendations.
Option D (incorrect) is Amazon Comprehend, a natural language processing service, not for recommendations.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain49_10',
  NOW(),
  100,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_49_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_49_m_49_2_50',
  'A media company wants to create audio versions of their news articles for visually impaired users. They need a service that can convert text content into natural-sounding speech in multiple languages. Which AWS service is specifically designed for this purpose?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon Transcribe","Amazon Polly","Amazon Comprehend","Amazon Lex"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (Amazon Polly) is a text-to-speech service that turns text into lifelike speech, allowing you to create applications that talk and build entirely new categories of speech-enabled products. It supports multiple languages and various voices. Option A (Amazon Transcribe) is a speech-to-text service, converting audio into text, which is the opposite of the requirement. Option C (Amazon Comprehend) is a natural language processing (NLP) service that uses machine learning to find insights and relationships in text, such as sentiment analysis or entity recognition, but it does not convert text to speech. Option D (Amazon Lex) is a service for building conversational interfaces (chatbots, voice assistants) using voice and text, but its primary function is not text-to-speech conversion for general content.',
  NOW(),
