  'Before comparison, each model''s performance must be quantified. Option C (Evaluate each model on a validation dataset) provides the necessary performance data. Option A (Compare model evaluation metrics (e.g., AUC-ROC, F1 score)) then allows for a direct comparison of their accuracy or predictive power. To consider cost, Option B (Estimate inference costs for each model) is essential. Finally, Option D (Select the model that balances performance and cost-effectiveness) makes the final decision based on all gathered information.',
