  'The first step in setting up an A/B test is to clearly define the objective. Option D (Determine the hypothesis to be tested) establishes this. Following that, Option A (Define the primary metric) specifies how success will be measured. Option C (Deploy the new model and the existing model) makes the models available for testing. Finally, Option B (Randomly split the user traffic) ensures that the experiment groups are statistically comparable, allowing for unbiased evaluation.',
