  'A clear problem statement is the foundation. Option D (Formulate the problem statement clearly) ensures everyone understands the goal. Option B (Define clear, quantifiable success metrics) makes the problem measurable. Option A (Identify available data sources and their quality) determines if the problem is solvable with existing data. Finally, Option C (Establish a baseline performance without ML) provides a benchmark to assess the ML solution''s value.',
