  '{0,2,1,3}',
  'Model selection begins with a deep understanding of the problem and data. Option A (Understand the problem type and data characteristics) is the foundational step. Based on this understanding, Option B (Shortlist candidate models) narrows down the choices. Before final evaluation, Option C (Consider model complexity, interpretability, and computational resources) adds practical constraints to the decision. Finally, Option D (Evaluate shortlisted models) provides empirical evidence for the best choice.',
