  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'The choice between linear models and XGBoost often starts with data characteristics. Option A (Assess the linearity of relationships) directly informs whether a linear model is sufficient. Option B (Consider the need for model interpretability) highlights a key advantage of linear models. Option C (Evaluate the dataset size and potential for complex interactions) points to scenarios where XGBoost excels. Finally, Option D (Choose XGBoost for higher accuracy... or a linear model for simplicity) summarizes the decision criteria.',
