  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'Model selection for customer churn starts with defining the problem. Option A (Determine that the problem is binary classification) categorizes the task. Next, Option B (Consider models known for tabular data and classification) narrows down the choices to suitable algorithms. Option C (Evaluate the importance of interpretability versus predictive accuracy) introduces a crucial business constraint. Finally, Option D (Select the model that best balances interpretability, accuracy, and training/inference speed) makes the informed decision.',
