  '{0,2,1,3}',
  'The suitability of an LLM begins with the complexity of the task. Option A (Assess if the task involves complex language understanding) is the primary indicator. Next, Option C (Determine if the task can benefit from pre-trained knowledge) highlights a core advantage of LLMs. Option B (Consider the computational resources and cost) addresses the practical implications of using LLMs. Finally, Option D (Evaluate if a smaller, specialized model could achieve sufficient performance) acts as a crucial check to avoid over-engineering.',
