  '{1,0,2,3}',
  'Building a recommendation system starts with understanding the data. Option A (Analyze available data) is crucial for informing subsequent choices. Next, Option B (Identify the type of recommendation) defines the strategic approach. Option C (Consider the scale of users and items) introduces important performance and resource constraints. Finally, Option D (Shortlist models based on data type, recommendation type, and scalability needs) narrows down the algorithmic options.',
