  'Understanding the framework''s capabilities is a good starting point. Option D (Identify the specific ML framework and its hardware acceleration support) informs hardware needs. Option A (Estimate the computational complexity of the model and dataset size) quantifies the workload. Option B (Choose between CPU-only or GPU instances based on complexity and cost) makes the initial resource decision. Finally, Option C (Benchmark different instance types with a small subset of data) validates the choice with empirical testing.',
