  'The first step is to define how error is measured. Option B (Select an appropriate loss function (e.g., Mean Squared Error, Cross-Entropy)) sets this. Option D (Feed input data through the model to get predictions) generates the model''s output. Option A (Calculate the difference between predicted and actual values) quantifies the error. Finally, Option C (Use the loss value to update model parameters via an optimizer) drives the learning process.',
