  '{0,3,1,2}',
  'Data splitting begins with ensuring randomness. Option A (Randomly shuffle the entire dataset) is crucial for unbiased splits. For classification tasks, Option D (Apply any necessary stratification) helps maintain class balance. Next, Option B (Separate a portion for the training set) creates the largest segment for model learning. Finally, Option C (Further split the remaining data) creates the validation set for hyperparameter tuning and the test set for final, unbiased evaluation.',
