VALUES (
  'q_49_m_49_3_80',
  'Arrange the steps to restrict public access to an Amazon S3 bucket containing sensitive ML training data.',
  'ordering',
  '["Block all public access settings at the S3 bucket level.","Ensure the S3 bucket policy does not grant public read/write access.","Review the S3 bucket''s Access Control Lists (ACLs) for public grants.","Verify that the S3 bucket is not configured as a static website."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'The most effective first step to restrict public access is to enable the ''Block all public access'' settings at the S3 bucket level (Option A), which provides a strong preventative control. Following this, you should ensure that the S3 bucket policy explicitly denies any public read or write access (Option B). Next, review the S3 bucket''s Access Control Lists (ACLs) to confirm no public grants exist (Option C). Finally, verify that the S3 bucket is not configured as a static website (Option D), as this inherently makes objects publicly accessible.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain49_10',
  NOW(),
  3,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_49_3',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_49_m_49_3_81',
  'Arrange the following steps in the correct order to configure an Amazon S3 bucket for secure storage of sensitive machine learning training data.',
  'ordering',
  '["Enable S3 Block Public Access settings for the bucket.","Create the Amazon S3 bucket in the desired AWS Region.","Configure a bucket policy to grant least privilege access to specific IAM roles.","Enable default encryption for the S3 bucket using AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS)."]'::json,
  '{1,0,3,2}',
  'To secure an Amazon S3 bucket, the first step is to create the bucket (Option B). Next, it is a best practice to enable S3 Block Public Access settings (Option A) to prevent accidental public exposure. After that, enable default encryption for the bucket (Option D) to ensure all objects are encrypted at rest. Finally, configure a bucket policy (Option C) to enforce fine-grained access control based on the principle of least privilege, allowing only authorized IAM roles to access the data.',
