VALUES (
  'q_49_m_49_3_87',
  'An ML engineer needs to set up secure access for an Amazon SageMaker notebook instance to an Amazon S3 bucket containing training data. Arrange the following steps in the correct order to achieve this using the principle of least privilege.',
  'ordering',
  '["Attach the IAM policy to a new or existing IAM role.","Create an IAM policy that grants read-only access to the specific S3 bucket.","Specify the IAM role when creating or updating the SageMaker notebook instance.","Ensure the S3 bucket policy does not explicitly deny access to the IAM role."]'::json,
  '{1,0,2,3}',
  'To set up secure access with least privilege, the first step is to create a specific IAM policy (Option B) that defines the exact permissions needed (read-only to the S3 bucket). Next, this policy must be attached to an IAM role (Option A) that SageMaker can assume. The SageMaker notebook instance is then configured to use this IAM role (Option C). Finally, it''s crucial to verify that no existing S3 bucket policies (Option D) are overriding or explicitly denying the permissions granted by the IAM role, which could prevent access.',
