VALUES (
  'q_49_m_49_3_89',
  'An organization wants to restrict network access to Amazon SageMaker notebook instances and training jobs within a private network. Order the steps to achieve this using an Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (Amazon VPC).',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure security groups to control inbound and outbound traffic for the SageMaker resources.","Create a new Amazon VPC with private subnets.","Specify the VPC and private subnets when launching SageMaker notebook instances and training jobs.","Configure VPC endpoints for SageMaker and S3 to allow private communication."]'::json,
  '{1,3,0,2}',
  'To restrict network access, first, a new Amazon VPC with private subnets (Option B) must be created to isolate the network environment. Next, VPC endpoints for SageMaker and S3 (Option D) are essential to allow private communication between SageMaker resources and S3 without traversing the public internet. After that, security groups (Option A) are configured to act as virtual firewalls, controlling traffic to and from the SageMaker resources within the VPC. Finally, when launching SageMaker notebook instances and training jobs, the created VPC and private subnets must be specified (Option C) to ensure they operate within this isolated network.',
