  'The process begins by choosing ''Create alarm'' in the CloudWatch console (Option C). Next, you must select the appropriate metric, which involves navigating to the ''AWS/SageMaker'' namespace and specifying the ''Endpoint'' dimension for your SageMaker endpoint (Option A). After selecting the metric, you define the threshold that triggers the alarm, such as CPU utilization exceeding 70% (Option B). Finally, you configure an Amazon SNS topic (Option D) to receive notifications when the alarm state is reached, ensuring timely alerts.',
