VALUES (
  'q_49_m_49_1_75',
  'Arrange the steps to enable basic Auto Scaling for a SageMaker endpoint to handle varying inference loads.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure the scaling policy, defining target utilization and min/max instances.","Register the SageMaker endpoint variant with Application Auto Scaling.","Define the custom metric for scaling, such as ''InvocationsPerInstance''.","Create the SageMaker endpoint with multiple instances."]'::json,
  '{3,1,2,0}',
  'The first step is to create the Amazon SageMaker endpoint, ensuring it is configured with multiple instances to allow for scaling (Option D). Next, you must register the specific SageMaker endpoint variant with Application Auto Scaling (Option B), making it eligible for automatic scaling. After registration, you define the custom metric that Auto Scaling will monitor, such as ''InvocationsPerInstance'' (Option C), to determine when to scale. Finally, you configure the scaling policy (Option A), specifying the target utilization for the metric and the minimum and maximum number of instances allowed.',
