  '{2,3,0,1}',
  'The initial step is to create a new Application Load Balancer (ALB) in the EC2 console (Option C). Next, you specify the Amazon VPC, subnets, and security groups (Option D) where the ALB will operate. After the ALB is set up, you create a target group and register your ML inference Amazon EC2 instances with it (Option A), defining where the ALB will send traffic. Finally, you configure listener rules (Option B) for the ALB to forward incoming requests to the appropriate target group, distributing the inference load.',
