  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'To deploy a highly available SageMaker endpoint, first create a SageMaker model resource (Option A) by providing the model artifacts and inference code. Next, create an endpoint configuration (Option B) where you define the instance types, count, and specify production variants, ensuring they are distributed across multiple Availability Zones for resiliency. Then, deploy the endpoint (Option C) using this configuration. Finally, monitor the endpoint''s health and performance (Option D) with Amazon CloudWatch to ensure continuous operation and detect issues.',
