VALUES (
  'q_49_m_49_4_85',
  'An ML team needs to compare the performance of two different versions of a machine learning model in production using A/B testing with Amazon SageMaker. Order the steps to set up this test.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an Amazon SageMaker endpoint configuration with two ProductionVariants, each referencing a different model version.","Update the existing Amazon SageMaker endpoint to use the new endpoint configuration, specifying traffic distribution.","Deploy the two different model versions as separate Amazon SageMaker model resources.","Monitor the performance metrics (e.g., accuracy, latency) for each ProductionVariant to compare models."]'::json,
  '{2,0,1,3}',
  'To set up A/B testing, first, deploy the two different model versions as separate Amazon SageMaker model resources (Option C). Next, create an Amazon SageMaker endpoint configuration (Option A) that includes two ProductionVariants, with each variant referencing one of the model versions. Then, update the existing Amazon SageMaker endpoint (Option B) to use this new endpoint configuration, specifying the desired traffic distribution (e.g., 50/50) between the two variants. Finally, monitor the performance metrics (Option D) for each ProductionVariant to evaluate and compare the models'' real-world performance.',
