  '{1,0,2,3}',
  'To monitor inference latency, first, deploy the Amazon SageMaker real-time inference endpoint (Option B) so that it begins generating metrics. Next, access the Amazon CloudWatch console (Option A) and navigate to the SageMaker metrics section, where endpoint performance data is automatically published. Then, identify the ''ModelLatency'' metric (Option C) specifically associated with your deployed endpoint. Finally, create a CloudWatch alarm (Option D) configured to trigger if this ''ModelLatency'' metric exceeds your defined SLA threshold, providing proactive alerts.',
