  '{1,3,2,0}',
  'To prepare a tabular dataset for SageMaker, the first step is to load the raw data from Amazon S3 (Option B) into a suitable processing environment. Next, clean and preprocess the data (Option D), which involves handling missing values, outliers, and converting data types. Then, perform feature engineering (Option C), such as one-hot encoding categorical features or scaling numerical features, as required by the chosen SageMaker built-in algorithm. Finally, split the prepared dataset (Option A) into training, validation, and test sets, which are essential for model development and evaluation.',
